INT. GRUYERES AGING CELLAR - NIGHT

A limestone cave lit by work lamps. Ten thousand wheels of cheese on spruce shelves, rising in towers to the vault. The air smells of ammonia and cold stone.

PETRA VOLKOVA, 40s, crew boss, headlamp, climbing harness. MILOS DRAGIC, 30s, rigger, clips a carabiner. AKIKO TANABE, 20s, hacker, crouched over a ruggedised laptop on a cheese crate. NAILAH ROSS, 30s, driver, stands at the cellar door with a thermal flask.

PETRA
Report.

AKIKO
Cameras on a loop. Eleven minutes of grace.

MILOS
Eleven is plenty.

NAILAH
Truck's at the barn. Engine warm.

PETRA
Miloš, rope.

He tosses a coil. She catches it. Anchors it to a pillar. Tests the tension with her whole weight.

AKIKO
The vault door is on a thermal sensor. If it drops below four degrees, it locks.

MILOS
It's twelve in here.

AKIKO
It's twelve out here. Inside it's six.

PETRA
Then we bring a heater.

NAILAH
I've got a heater.

She lifts a silver case. Opens it. A compact space heater.

NAILAH (CONT'D)
Brought two.

MILOS
You think of everything.

NAILAH
I think of heaters.

PETRA
Akiko, how long on the lock?

AKIKO
Four minutes.

PETRA
Make it three.

AKIKO
Make me a coffee.

NAILAH
You want coffee?

AKIKO
I want three minutes. Coffee is a metaphor.

MILOS
It's a good one.

They move to the vault door. A circular steel hatch set into the rock, rimed with frost. Petra runs a glove over it.

PETRA
Seventeen wheels in there, aged forty years. Each one worth a Porsche.

MILOS
They smell like feet.

NAILAH
Porsches don't.

PETRA
Focus.

Akiko plugs a cable. Taps a key. The hatch ticks.

AKIKO
Two minutes forty.

MILOS
That was fast.

AKIKO
It's a cheap lock. They trusted the cheese.

PETRA
Miloš, harness.

He steps in. Petra clips him on. Akiko cracks the hatch.

Cold air floods out. Inside, the wheels gleam amber in the work lamps.

MILOS
(whispering)
Beautiful.

NAILAH
Don't sing to it.

PETRA
Nailah, the dolly.

She rolls it over. Together they lift the first wheel, a hundred pounds of rind and rot. It sits on the dolly like a sleeping animal.

AKIKO
Eight minutes left.

PETRA
Faster.

MILOS
I've got it.

NAILAH
I've got the second.

They work. A rhythm. Grunts, breath, the click of the dolly.

PETRA
Third.

MILOS
Third.

AKIKO
Seven minutes.

NAILAH
Fourth.

PETRA
Good.

Lamplight swings across the stacked wheels. A distant sound. All four stop.

NAILAH
(whisper)
Was that the door?

AKIKO
Cat.

PETRA
There's no cat.

AKIKO
Cat in the barn.

PETRA
(a beat)
Keep working.

They keep working. Fifth wheel. Sixth.

AKIKO
Five minutes.

MILOS
Seventh.

NAILAH
We have room for nine.

PETRA
Then we take nine.

They load. The truck horn, faint, beeps twice from outside. All four glance up.

PETRA (CONT'D)
That's the signal. Out.

They dismantle the rig. Rope coils. Lamp clicks off. The vault door seals.

They file out into the night, one wheel short of nine, and none of them says so.
